1. QURAN ROMAN URDU TRANSLITERATION TEXT (`data/roman-urdu/`)

PROPRIETARY — NOT OPEN SOURCE. All rights reserved.

No licence is granted to any person or organisation to use, copy, modify,
publish, distribute, sublicense, or create derivative works from the text in
`data/roman-urdu/`, in whole or in part, without the prior express written
permission of Al Marfa Technologies (owner: Mohammad Arif,
arif.mohammed@gmail.com).

This text is the transliteration itself: the vowelization choices, house
style (per `docs/decisions/0004-*.md`), and izafat/homograph judgment calls
applied to the underlying (public-domain) Urdu translation. That editorial
and creative labor is original expression belonging to Al Marfa Technologies,
distinct from the public-domain words it renders — see ATTRIBUTION.md for the
full basis, and the SCOPE note below for what this does and does not cover.

Current status: every verse is `beta-unverified` (see README.md "Status") —
nothing has been human-reviewed end to end. This closed licence reflects that
experimental status, not a permanent stance: once review clears a meaningful
portion of the text, the owner intends to revisit this licence (most likely
toward a permissive or share-alike release, consistent with this project's
"open lexicon" orientation elsewhere in the repo). Until that happens, treat
this text as fully reserved. Permission requests: contact the owner.

This proprietary claim mirrors the one already recorded for this same text
once ingested downstream, in `../alquran-data/LICENSE` and
`../alquran-data/ATTRIBUTION.md` (`resources.slug = ur-roman-abu-rayyan`) —
the two files should be kept in sync if either changes.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. THE LEXICON (`data/lexicon/`)

CC BY-SA 4.0 (inherited from the Dakshina dataset, accepted per
`docs/decisions/0001-roman-urdu-source-selection.md`). This is the
project's open deliverable — see `data/lexicon/LICENSE` for the full text
and required attribution (Roark, Wolf-Sonkin, Kirov, Mielke, Johny,
Demirşahin & Hall (2020), *Processing South Asian Languages Written in the
Latin Script: the Dakshina Dataset*, LREC).

Do not attach the CC BY-SA notice to material outside `data/lexicon/` — in
particular, it does not apply to `data/roman-urdu/` (§1 above).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. PIPELINE CODE (`scripts/`, `tests/`) AND DOCUMENTATION

Licence: undecided. Until a licence is chosen, no rights are granted beyond
what is needed to read this repository — treat as "all rights reserved" by
default, same reservation as §1, pending an explicit decision by the owner.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SCOPE — THIS NOTICE DOES NOT GRANT OR CLAIM RIGHTS OVER THE SOURCE TEXT.

Section 1's reservation covers Al Marfa Technologies' own transliteration
work, not the underlying Urdu translation it is derived from. The Junagarhi
Urdu translation is public domain (translator d. 1941; see ATTRIBUTION.md)
and cannot be claimed by anyone, including Al Marfa Technologies. Nothing in
this notice restricts use of the Junagarhi Urdu text itself, or of the
Qur'anic Arabic — only this repository's own Roman Urdu rendering of it.
